<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-20T05:02:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ebola: DR Congo outbreak not slowing, MSF warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e51ae5e0b8b6c3f8d92748e49338b4650c0a85e61bea65bd0ffb89decaf073d7</id><updated>2026-09-20T05:02:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719--f40efdc02bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors Without Borders has warned against premature optimism amid the DRC's largest-ever Ebola outbreak. "The outbreak is not shrinking, it is moving," an MSF official said, entering new and more underprepared regions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Protests erupt over deaths of 37 miners in custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a2b4fee544e95f739115a55254d6ad4d5292658e0dd66be96075741c94116d5</id><updated>2026-09-20T05:02:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-protests-erupt-over-deaths-of-37-miners-in-custody/a-79316847--075eb6c61d78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-protests-erupt-over-deaths-of-37-miners-in-custody/a-79316847?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of suspects accused of illegal mining were found dead in custody in Nigeria's north-central Niger State. Officials blame disease, while reports cite overcrowding and poor ventilation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola epidemic may have gone undetected for months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a0ce36748491a6f1dda4c3344435c688ae3b1bd9aef122bde03ca344e0960c7</id><updated>2026-09-20T05:02:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803--d84e2884bf66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deadliest Ebola outbreak on record in the Democratic Republic of Congo may have begun months before it was first declared in May.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a386fb9b979983b173d0cfb972e635f20052380b8c7fb4164a23eb4292f8a5</id><updated>2026-09-20T05:02:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12f94d32b1c23717f3b19066593b9ca1216180390fdfa2393d91fd67721e90cc</id><updated>2026-09-20T05:02:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
